  <prompt>Create `hooks/useRecordHeaderFields.ts` in the shared library by hoisting the R1 form-buffer machinery out of `MatterHeaderView.tsx`: form-buffer staging (`getXrmPage().getAttribute(n).setValue(v)`, lines 175-235), the pending-changes buffer + `pendingX[name] ?? values?.[name]` display resolution (lines 166-172 and 249-256), and `projectLookup()` (lines 145-155). While hoisting, UNIFY the missing-attribute path so BOTH text and lookup saves THROW `Field '…' not on form` — today `saveText` throws (line 185) but `saveLookup` (lines 220-227) only `console.warn`s and silently no-ops, dropping the user's edit. This is FR-13, FR-14, FR-19.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. React hooks for PCF-hosted shared components; Xrm form-buffer (`Xrm.Page.getAttribute().setValue()`) dirty-state pattern. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A shared `useRecordHeaderFields` hook exists in `@spaarke/ui-components` reproducing R1's v1.0.7 form-buffer semantics EXACTLY, with the missing-attribute path throwing for both text and lookup saves, unit-tested; the generic RecordHeader control (task 033) and OOB lookup cell (task 023) can consume it. MatterHeaderView itself is NOT migrated.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-13/FR-14/FR-19. R1 learned the hard way (v1.0.7): writing straight to Dataverse via `Xrm.WebApi.updateRecord` triggered a retrieveRecord round-trip that toggled the shell's loading skeleton and re-rendered the whole PCF on every edit. The fix — stage edits into the FORM buffer so the field goes dirty and the form's own Save commits — is a MUST rule in the spec ("MUST preserve R1's form-buffer dirty-state pattern exactly"). Without the hoist, ~82 lines of this machinery get copied into every future consumer, and the `saveLookup` silent-drop defect (FR-14) ships in each copy. Hoisting `Xrm.Page` access into `hooks/` does NOT break ADR-012 — the shared lib already does exactly this (`FieldMappingHandler`, `useRecordFieldValues`, `useRelatedCount`): components stay props-driven; Xrm access lives in hooks/services behind the window/parent walker (spec "ADR Tensions" point 2). Do not "fix" this placement.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useRecordHeaderFields.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/index.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/__tests__/useRecordHeaderFields.test.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/pcf/MatterHeader/control/MatterHeaderView.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useRecordFieldValues.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">Shared `getXrmPage()` in `utils/xrmContext.ts` — the hook MUST use it, never a local walker</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec-MUST">Every save in this hook stages via the form buffer (`getXrmPage().getAttribute(name).setValue(value)`). The hook MUST NOT call `Xrm.WebApi.updateRecord`, MUST NOT trigger a refetch after staging, and MUST NOT toggle any loading state on save — staged edits become visible ONLY through the pending buffer (R1 v1.0.7 semantics, preserved exactly).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-14">Both `saveText` and `saveLookup` THROW `new Error("Field '&lt;name&gt;' not on form")` when the attribute is absent, and throw when `Xrm.Page` is unavailable — the lookup path's current warn-and-return (MatterHeaderView.tsx:220-227) is the defect being fixed. No silent no-op survives in either path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-13">Display resolution is `pendingText[name] ?? values?.[name]` for text and — preserving the `'name' in pendingLookup` membership check from MatterHeaderView.tsx:253-256 — `name in pendingLookup ? pendingLookup[name] : projectLookup(values, name)` for lookups, so a staged CLEAR (pending `null`) displays as empty rather than falling back to the Dataverse-loaded value. Both buffers reset when `recordId` changes (lines 169-172) and at no other time.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="this task">Do NOT modify `MatterHeaderView.tsx` or any MatterHeader PCF file. The old control keeps its local machinery until its retirement (task 081); the hook's first consumers are tasks 023/033. Generalize field names (no `sprk_matter*` or `LOOKUP_META` hard-coding): `saveLookup` takes the target `entityType` as a parameter, since metadata-derived targets arrive via task 020's client, not via constants.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Xrm access goes exclusively through `getXrm()` / `getXrmPage()` from `utils/xrmContext.ts` (task 021). No local window-walker, no PCF-specific `ComponentFramework` types in the hook.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">React 16/17-safe: no `use()`, no `useSyncExternalStore`, no `createRoot`; `React.useState`/`useCallback`/`useEffect` only, imported as `* as React`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">All Dataverse read I/O stays inside `useRecordFieldValues` (Xrm.WebApi); no raw `fetch`, no `@spaarke/auth`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Form-buffer dirty-state hook</topic>
