    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Source machinery (copy semantics verbatim)" location="src/client/pcf/MatterHeader/control/MatterHeaderView.tsx">Lines 145-155 `projectLookup` (reads `_field_value` + `@OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue` keys); 166-172 pending buffers + recordId reset; 174-191 `saveText` (throwing path — the model for BOTH paths); 216-235 `saveLookup` (fix its non-throwing path; keep the `[{ id, name, entityType }]` / `null`-clears setValue payload shape from line 229-231); 248-256 display resolution incl. the `in` check.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Read hook to compose" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useRecordFieldValues.ts">The existing shared read path — the new hook composes it (or accepts its `values`/`loading` output) rather than duplicating retrieval. Mirror its test approach in `hooks/__tests__/useRecordFieldValues.test.ts`.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare RIGOR LEVEL FULL per CLAUDE.md §8; update current-task.md.</step>
    <step order="1">Design the hook signature: input `{ entity, recordId, fields }` (composing `useRecordFieldValues` internally) returning `{ values, loading, saveText(name, value), saveLookup(name, item, entityType), displayText(name), displayLookup(name) }` — or an equivalent shape that keeps every FR-13 semantic. Export `projectLookup` as a named pure function for unit testing.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement staging: both save paths obtain the page via the shared `getXrmPage()` (task 021), throw `Form buffer unavailable` when it is null, throw `Field '&lt;name&gt;' not on form` when `getAttribute` returns nothing, then `setValue` + update the matching pending buffer. Lookup payload: `[{ id, name, entityType }]`, `null` clears.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement pending buffers + display resolution + recordId-change reset exactly per the FR-13 constraint above.</step>
    <step order="4">Export the hook (and `projectLookup`) from `hooks/index.ts`.</step>
    <step order="5">Author `hooks/__tests__/useRecordHeaderFields.test.ts` covering every acceptance criterion below (mock `window.Xrm.Page` with jest attribute stubs; mirror the existing hook tests' renderHook approach).</step>
    <step order="6">Build the shared lib and run its full test suite; green.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the form-buffer semantics cannot be preserved EXACTLY in a shared hook — any design pressure toward staging-triggered refetch, loading toggles, buffer resets outside recordId change, or loosening the `'name' in pendingLookup` cleared-value semantics — STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than adapting the semantics. Writing straight to Dataverse re-rendered the whole PCF (R1 v1.0.7); this failure mode is the reason the task exists.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>None found for save/staging machinery in the shared lib — spec §11 table records "useRecordHeaderFields / RecordHeaderFields — none (grep-verified)". The machinery exists only inside the PCF layer at `MatterHeaderView.tsx:145-256`; the closest shared neighbors are `hooks/useRecordFieldValues.ts` (read-only retrieval, no staging) and `hooks/useRecordHeaderToolbarActions.ts` (toolbar only).</existing>
    <extension>No — `useRecordFieldValues` is the read path and contains no form-buffer/pending-state surface, and the source implementation lives in a PCF view file that the shared library cannot import and that is scheduled for retirement (task 081). The new hook composes `useRecordFieldValues` rather than duplicating it.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Each of the R2 rollout consumers (RecordHeader control task 033, and any future header surface) would re-copy ~82 lines of staging/pending/projection machinery per consumer, and the `saveLookup` silent-drop defect (FR-14 — a user's lookup edit is warn-logged and discarded when the field is not on the form) ships again in every copy.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build shared lib (`npm run build`) and run tests (`npm test`) in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components</tool>
  </tools>

