  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a field present on the form, when `saveText(name, v)` runs, then the mocked attribute's `setValue` is called with `v`, the pending buffer holds `v`, `displayText(name)` returns `v`, and NO `Xrm.WebApi.updateRecord` / re-retrieve occurs (mock call counts prove it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a lookup field present on the form, when `saveLookup(name, item, entityType)` runs, then `setValue` receives `[{ id, name, entityType }]`; when called with `null`, `setValue` receives `null` and `displayLookup(name)` returns the cleared (empty) state even though `values` still holds the Dataverse value (the `in`-check semantics).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a field NOT on the form (`getAttribute` returns null/undefined), BOTH `saveText` and `saveLookup` throw an Error whose message contains `Field '&lt;name&gt;' not on form` — neither path warn-and-returns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given `Xrm.Page` unavailable on every frame, BOTH save paths throw (no silent no-op).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given staged pending values, when `recordId` changes, then both pending buffers reset to empty; unrelated re-renders with the same `recordId` do NOT reset them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`projectLookup(values, field)` returns `{ id, name }` from `_field_value` + its FormattedValue annotation, and `null` for missing/empty id — unit-tested as a pure function.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The hook module imports `getXrmPage` from `../utils/xrmContext` (no local window-walker) and contains no `sprk_`-prefixed field or entity constants.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git diff` shows no change under `src/client/pcf/MatterHeader/`; shared-lib build and full test suite green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec refs: FR-13, FR-14, FR-19; spec MUST rule "preserve R1's form-buffer dirty-state pattern exactly"; R1 v1.0.7 history in MatterHeaderView.tsx header comment (lines 8-22). The FR-19 companion component `RecordHeaderFields.tsx` (grid composition) is Phase 3 scope (task 033 wiring), not this task. Task 023 adds the OOB-picker staging on top of this hook's `saveLookup`.</notes>

