    <form-buffer-semantics-preserved>
      Every save stages via `getXrmPage().getAttribute(name).setValue(value)`. NO `Xrm.WebApi.updateRecord`
      (grep-verified absent + guard-tested); NO refetch after staging (`retrieveRecord` call count pinned at 1
      across multiple saves); NO loading toggle on save (`loading` sampled during and after a save, asserted
      false throughout); `refresh` deliberately NOT re-exported from the result so a consumer cannot
      reintroduce the round trip (guard-tested). Buffers reset on `recordId` change ONLY — proven both ways
      (resets on change; does NOT reset on a same-recordId re-render with a new `fields` array reference).
      The `'name' in pendingLookup` membership check is preserved verbatim, so a staged CLEAR displays empty
      rather than falling back to the still-loaded Dataverse value.
    </form-buffer-semantics-preserved>
    <deviations>
      <deviation kind="logging">R1's `console.warn`(before throw) / `console.info`(staged edit) replaced by the
        shared `createLogger` (`utils/logger.ts`) at debug level — the shared-lib convention, cf.
        `services/FieldMappingHandler.ts`. The warn-before-throw was redundant with the thrown message.
        Logging is not a form-buffer semantic; staging behavior is byte-identical. Documented in the file header.</deviation>
      <deviation kind="type-only">`displayText` returns `string | null | undefined` rather than R1's
        `as string | undefined` cast. Zero runtime change — it is simply truthful about the `null` Dataverse
        genuinely returns for empty fields, and is assignable to BOTH `TextField.value`
        (`string|number|null|undefined`) and `TextareaField.value` (`string|null|undefined`).</deviation>
      <deviation kind="additive">`error` added to the result — a pass-through of `useRecordFieldValues`'s
        existing error, so task 033 can render a degraded state on read failure. Not new surface.</deviation>
      <deviation kind="scope-held">Scope held to `saveText` + `saveLookup` per the closed acceptance set. The
        Boolean/Date/Number/OptionSet renderers' `onSave` take `boolean` / `Date|null` / `number|null` — task 033
        will need staging for those value types. A generic `saveValue` was deliberately NOT added: new surface
        outside this task's criteria (CLAUDE.md §11). Routed to 033.</deviation>
      <deviation kind="not-harmonised">`getXrmPage()`'s 2-frame walk vs `getXrm()`'s 3-frame walk was left AS-IS
        (task 021's deliberate choice). Assessed and it does not matter for this hook: a form-embedded
        RecordHeader PCF has Xrm on frame 1, a Code Page host on frame 2. Only a host nested deeper than one
        iframe would read fine (3-frame `getXrm`) but fail to stage (2-frame `getXrmPage`) — no such consumer
        exists. The asymmetry is documented in the hook's file header for whoever hits it first.</deviation>
      <deviation kind="artifact">POML step 8 asked for a deviation note under `notes/`. Recorded here in the POML
        plus in the hook's file-header JSDoc instead (durable, co-located with the code). No `notes/` acceptance
        criterion exists, and the executing agent was directed not to create standalone report .md files.</deviation>
    </deviations>
